I compared CarePoint with PowerSchool, Veracross, Gradelink, openSIS, SchoolTry, and Ed-admin.

## What Standard SMS Products Offer

Common systems focus on:

- Student records and enrollment
- Attendance
- Gradebook and report cards
- Admissions
- Parent portals
- Fee billing and online payments
- Communication
- Scheduling
- Health and behavior records
- Custom reports
- Mobile access
- Accounting/LMS integrations
- Role-based security

Examples:

- [PowerSchool SIS](https://www.powerschool.com/solutions/student-information-system/) emphasizes connected data, reporting, family engagement, integrations, and analytics.
- [Veracross](https://www.veracross.com/solutions/) emphasizes one database across admissions, academics, finance, portals, and communications.
- [Gradelink](https://www.gradelink.com/features/) offers gradebooks, standards-based grading, attendance, report cards, tuition, parent access, messaging, health, behavior, and integrations.
- [openSIS](https://www.opensis.com/features/) includes custom student fields, health, scheduling, grading, billing, scholarships, statements, payments, reminders, messaging, and advanced reporting.
- [Ed-admin](https://www.ed-admin.com/) positions itself around one connected platform, multiple portals, AI assistance, and eliminating disconnected school systems.
- [SchoolTry](https://schooltry.com/) focuses on African school operations, attendance, grading, parent communication, and cloud access.

